WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.263 --> 00:00:03.263
(groovy jazz music)

00:00:12.533 --> 00:00:13.836
- So today we're getting transformed

00:00:13.836 --> 00:00:15.841
into our hero musicians.

00:00:15.841 --> 00:00:18.415
I'm going to try a look
inspired by Amy Winehouse

00:00:18.415 --> 00:00:19.885
because I love her.

00:00:19.885 --> 00:00:21.923
You can here in her music
that she was so honest

00:00:21.923 --> 00:00:23.429
and that she was being herself

00:00:23.429 --> 00:00:25.145
with every lyric that she wrote

00:00:25.145 --> 00:00:27.018
and every song that she put out.

00:00:27.018 --> 00:00:28.566
Some of her songs were uplifting.

00:00:28.566 --> 00:00:30.359
Some of her songs were sad, but

00:00:30.359 --> 00:00:31.911
that was the reality of her.

00:00:31.911 --> 00:00:34.271
- Amy Winehouse was so compelling

00:00:34.271 --> 00:00:37.441
in part because she was able to

00:00:37.441 --> 00:00:38.691
somehow combine

00:00:39.966 --> 00:00:42.254
a certain type of confident

00:00:42.254 --> 00:00:46.665
imperfection with a
very humble virtuosity.

00:00:46.665 --> 00:00:49.795
- Today, I'm being
transformed into John Lennon.

00:00:49.795 --> 00:00:52.893
So John Lennon is probably
the only person who

00:00:52.893 --> 00:00:56.933
gives me the chills every
time I hear any of his songs.

00:00:56.933 --> 00:01:00.116
My dad just played him over
and over and over again.

00:01:00.116 --> 00:01:02.886
It's like a very nostalgic,
emotional connection

00:01:02.886 --> 00:01:05.948
I have with Lennon that I don't
have with any other artist.

00:01:05.948 --> 00:01:09.856
- I think Lennon's longevity
in the public imagination

00:01:09.856 --> 00:01:11.613
and in our listening practices

00:01:11.613 --> 00:01:14.473
has a lot to do with the
style of his song-writing,

00:01:14.473 --> 00:01:16.104
that he was constantly innovating

00:01:16.104 --> 00:01:19.244
and attempting to develop new means

00:01:19.244 --> 00:01:22.582
for us to actually understand
the world around us.

00:01:22.582 --> 00:01:25.800
- Today, I'm gonna be dressed
in a Pharrell-inspired look.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.638
He's pretty much one
of the greatest humans

00:01:27.638 --> 00:01:29.067
to ever walk the earth.

00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:32.545
Pharrell was, I feel
like, the first outlet to

00:01:32.545 --> 00:01:34.868
let me be able to be myself.

00:01:34.868 --> 00:01:36.127
He's incredible.

00:01:36.127 --> 00:01:37.924
- So, in particular in the hip-hop genre,

00:01:37.924 --> 00:01:39.798
there's a certain perceived notion

00:01:39.798 --> 00:01:41.881
or stereotype of black masculinity

00:01:41.881 --> 00:01:44.410
as always aggressive,
and there are many, many

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:47.279
different ways in which hip-hop musicians

00:01:47.279 --> 00:01:49.812
have refused those types of labels

00:01:49.812 --> 00:01:51.767
and Pharrell is one of those people.

00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:53.847
- I'm a little worried about
what I'm gonna look like.

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:56.131
I mean, I'm down to try it out.

00:01:56.131 --> 00:01:59.631
(lively electronic music)

00:02:01.986 --> 00:02:04.552
The biggest thing, I think, is the hair.

00:02:04.552 --> 00:02:07.238
Obviously, she has this huge beehive

00:02:07.238 --> 00:02:09.561
and so I'm kind of on the fence of

00:02:09.561 --> 00:02:11.108
how it's gonna look on me.

00:02:11.108 --> 00:02:13.272
- Every time I saw
Pharrell, I just felt like

00:02:13.272 --> 00:02:14.985
I was looking at that cool uncle

00:02:14.985 --> 00:02:16.530
I always wanted to have.

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:18.488
I felt like when I
first put the jacket on,

00:02:18.488 --> 00:02:20.086
like that was the foundation.

00:02:20.086 --> 00:02:22.568
When the hat came out,
that's when it was just like,

00:02:22.568 --> 00:02:24.199
that's when it was done.

00:02:24.199 --> 00:02:28.168
- I think that I sometimes
accidentally dress like Lennon.

00:02:28.168 --> 00:02:30.899
So yeah, I would rock that look.

00:02:30.899 --> 00:02:35.277
His sunnies in particular,
but the middle part,

00:02:35.277 --> 00:02:36.895
it's not in right now.

00:02:36.895 --> 00:02:38.061
He pulled it off.

00:02:38.061 --> 00:02:40.279
- I'm not very used to
wearing bright lip colors,

00:02:40.279 --> 00:02:43.397
so this is something that's
definitely very weird for me.

00:02:43.397 --> 00:02:45.515
When we brought the wig over, I was like

00:02:45.515 --> 00:02:48.165
"That is not going to fit on my head."

00:02:48.165 --> 00:02:50.247
We definitely tried and we got it on.

00:02:50.247 --> 00:02:51.643
It's on my head.

00:02:51.643 --> 00:02:53.359
- [Tan] I hope it's gonna look cool.

00:02:53.359 --> 00:02:56.254
I hope I do him some kind of justice

00:02:56.254 --> 00:03:00.421
and I hope my dad sees this
and he's happy with it.

00:03:01.961 --> 00:03:05.752
(upbeat dance music)

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:09.221
Lying around with flower
petals being thrown at my face.

00:03:09.221 --> 00:03:10.304
What a dream.

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:13.547
- [Curtis] I definitely think
that the aesthetic today,

00:03:13.547 --> 00:03:15.504
I think Pharrell approves of this.

00:03:15.504 --> 00:03:16.975
When speaking about Pharrell,

00:03:16.975 --> 00:03:19.027
I don't even know if it's like dance.

00:03:19.027 --> 00:03:20.288
It's like groove.

00:03:20.288 --> 00:03:22.081
You find the beat and you ride it,

00:03:22.081 --> 00:03:23.899
and then you're just like, "Yeah.

00:03:23.899 --> 00:03:25.653
Yeah, this is it."

00:03:25.653 --> 00:03:26.984
(dance music)

00:03:26.984 --> 00:03:28.125
- [Selorm] I don't know
how it's gonna look,

00:03:28.125 --> 00:03:29.244
I don't know how I did.

00:03:29.244 --> 00:03:30.506
Internally, I feel so shy because

00:03:30.506 --> 00:03:32.542
I'm not used to just like, doing that.

00:03:32.542 --> 00:03:33.807
Because I listened to some of her music

00:03:33.807 --> 00:03:36.992
and just, like, tried to
appreciate who she was

00:03:36.992 --> 00:03:39.398
and the way that the
music always made me feel.

00:03:39.398 --> 00:03:41.070
Honestly, I had a lot of fun,

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:44.057
so I'm hoping that that's
conveyed through the video.

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:48.066
I'm excited to see it,
but only time will tell.

00:03:48.066 --> 00:03:50.358
(jazz music)

00:03:50.358 --> 00:03:53.327
- I didn't even know that a
reveal was part of this video.

00:03:53.327 --> 00:03:54.756
So this is kinda exciting, but I'm

00:03:54.756 --> 00:03:56.632
a little bit nervous, too, cuz

00:03:56.632 --> 00:03:58.464
I've got big shoes to fill.

00:03:58.464 --> 00:04:00.672
- I'm excited to see how it turned out.

00:04:00.672 --> 00:04:03.042
It was some really cool stuff happening.

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:05.814
The dance moves was there,
the vibes were there.

00:04:05.814 --> 00:04:08.137
The outfit was there, ya know?

00:04:08.137 --> 00:04:09.816
So I'm excited about it.

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:13.853
- I'm excited, but I also
hope I don't look crazy.

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:15.728
I really wanted this to be
something that honored her

00:04:15.728 --> 00:04:18.342
and was kind of a beautiful appreciation

00:04:18.342 --> 00:04:20.095
of what I appreciate about her.

00:04:20.095 --> 00:04:22.751
So I hope it comes off that way.

00:04:22.751 --> 00:04:25.584
- All right. I'm gonna press play.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:30.460
(Lennon-style electronic music)

00:04:36.821 --> 00:04:37.654
Yeah.

00:04:39.141 --> 00:04:41.224
Shit, that's fuckin cool.

00:04:43.017 --> 00:04:47.011
I look like a stoned lesbian John Lennon.

00:04:47.011 --> 00:04:48.344
This is perfect.

00:04:53.205 --> 00:04:54.955
Oh, man, I love this.

00:04:57.037 --> 00:04:59.769
That looked heaps better than I imagined.

00:04:59.769 --> 00:05:02.059
I am a little bit cool.

00:05:02.059 --> 00:05:03.411
I didn't know that.

00:05:03.411 --> 00:05:05.569
So I'm really excited for
