00:07:30.591 --> 00:07:33.244
I'm still not doing that hair
ever fucking again, though.

00:07:33.244 --> 00:07:34.589
I'm never doing that again.

00:07:34.589 --> 00:07:37.932
- The ways in which people
actually engage the music

00:07:37.932 --> 00:07:41.588
is suggestive, then, of how
they engage with the musicians.

00:07:41.588 --> 00:07:43.505
So music is a way in which people

00:07:43.505 --> 00:07:46.151
are often connected to
the world around them.

00:07:46.151 --> 00:07:47.983
And these musicians then become

00:07:47.983 --> 00:07:50.020
the conduit for our connections,

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:53.157
they become the ways in which
we can imagine ourselves

00:07:53.157 --> 00:07:55.123
thinking differently
or living differently,

00:07:55.123 --> 00:07:57.156
or being differently in the world.

00:07:57.156 --> 00:07:59.068
And so, people quite often have

00:07:59.068 --> 00:08:01.798
a very significant
attachment to the musicians

00:08:01.798 --> 00:08:05.298
that they listen to and whom they idolize.

00:08:06.206 --> 00:08:08.956
(rhythmic music)

